# Fe VI — ATTEMPT 1, SUBSTITUTED. NOT A CAPTURE. Register 1639.
# sent:        ...energy1.pl?spectrum=Fe+VI&units=0&format=2&conf_out=on...
# destination: ...energy1.pl?conf_out=on&format=2&j_out=on&level_out=on
#              &spectrum=Se+III&submit=Retrieve+Data&units=0
#
# ** MISMATCH. I asked for Fe VI and was served Se III's body. **
#
# This is register 1629's mechanism exactly: the permission layer serves
# a URL it already holds rather than the one requested. Se III was
# fetched in the immediately preceding turn, so its URL was the nearest
# permitted match.
#
# NOTHING WRITTEN. Had the destination_url not been checked, Se III's
# 51 levels would now be sitting in the tree under the name FeVI.tsv —
# a whole species of plausible, correctly-formatted, entirely wrong data.
#
# THE CHECK THAT CAUGHT IT is the one R 1638 made a rule before the
# first fetch: verify destination_url against what was sent BEFORE
# anything is written.
